invariant reading
1. The measured cyclic state word determines p0, L_y, p0+p1/7, single-sector bias, fold
   reciprocals, and all common-wall transfer shadows by quotienting or coupling.
2. Neutral measure can dominate a transfer while the signed result is decided by a small
   addressed residue of state pairs.  This matches HYP-2647's warning that balanced
   moving-sector marginals do not determine the obstruction.
3. The far-element plateau quotient only retains (p0,p1).  It is useful because it is
   monotone under KPS-style x-cell tails, but it discards transition adjacency and
   sector labels that the AP-to-defect wall proof needs.
4. Fold targets and coset/reciprocal signatures should be treated as addresses on the
   same finite state object, not as independent explanations.

tournament-analysis quotient
vertices: measured state word, signed state transport, missed-set histogram,
p0/p1 plateau, fold-target profile, mod-7 reciprocal phase, raw relation rank, raw runners
edge rule: A -> B when B is a deterministic quotient or valuation of A
Hamiltonian path: state word -> transport -> histogram -> plateau -> fold profile ->
mod-7 phase -> relation rank -> runners
challenged assumption: tournament vertices need not be runners or arcs; here they are
finite addresses and quotient obligations that preserve the LRC bad-set measure.
